<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="56da4227-4773-4148-ad83-e42e2702a677"><problem><para>
      <para> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2+10\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>19</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 19. \((-3)^2+10=9+10=19\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
