<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="414a4c79-f8ca-4d84-bdb0-3799b2d22150"><problem><para>
      <para> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(x^2-3\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>6</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 6. \((-3)^2-3=9-3=6\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<example><exercise>
  <problem> 
    <para>Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to see the solutions to questions 1 - 2 organized into a table.</para>
