<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="12964d60-9f81-4912-977d-ded91307039c"><problem><para>
      <para> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>4.5</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 4.5. \(\frac{1}{2}(-3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
